# MITIGA core rules

- Read `AGENTS.md` and the architecture and governance documents before coding.
- Product north: MITIGA is a configurable, explainable and auditable Customer Risk Assessment (CRA) and Due-Diligence engine for EU obliged entities. MITIGA does the work; the entity retains the decision. See `docs/product/PRODUCT-DIRECTION-MVP-25.md` and `docs/adr/0012-customer-cra-engine-as-mvp-core.md`.
- Roles: Claude (Cowork) orchestrates and reviews independently; Edu (human owner) approves and merges; Claude Code owns backend/domain work; Cursor owns the frontend. Task contracts are in `docs/tasks/`, review reports in `docs/reviews/`.
- Work from a bounded task contract with explicit acceptance criteria.
- Keep `main` deployable; use a short-lived branch and squash merge.
- The MVP is a modular monolith. New services require an ADR.
- English is the source language for UI copy, email, reports, code, API fields, commits, and technical identifiers.
- Follow ADR 0002 and externalize user-facing strings into typed message catalogs.
- Preserve the MITIGA design tokens and sober, low-contrast visual language.
- Never commit or paste secrets. Use `.env.local` and the deployment secret store.
- Every data path must enforce tenant isolation server-side.
- Every risk outcome must retain policy version, reasons, inputs provenance, and actor.
- Do not make unrelated changes or silently expand scope.
- Run relevant checks and return the handoff template from the governance document.
